<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H676</pnldref><english><title>Participate in a prison mutiny and fail to submit to lawful authority</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>riot</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>rioting</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>Prison Security Act 1992</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), being detained in lawful custody, while on the premises of **(..SPECIFY THE PRISON..) took part in a prison mutiny in that you failed, without reasonable excuse, to submit to lawful authority when you had or had been given reasonable opportunity to do so</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 1(1) of the Prison Security Act 1992.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;detained in lawful custody&lt;br /&gt; while on premises&lt;br /&gt; take part in a prison mutiny&lt;br /&gt; fail without reasonable excuse&lt;br /&gt; submit lawful authority&lt;br /&gt; given reasonable opportunity</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) The consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions is required.&lt;br /&gt; (ii) See section 1(6) for meaning of 'prison' and 'prisoner'.&lt;br /&gt; (iii) This offence is for 'failing to submit to authority', a variation for 'trying to overthrow authority' can be viewed at H655.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>IND</code><description>INDICTABLE</description></modeoftrial><consents><consent><code>D</code><description>DPP</description></consent></consents><timelimitforprosecutions>None</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Ten years imprisonment and / or a fine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;None</penalty><geographicregion><code>EW</code><description>England and Wales</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>PS92002</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>8.19.1.2</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>08